<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03F1">Remark <span data-tag="03F1">7.1.2.4</span> <span class="named">(Duality)</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a data-tag="03EY" href="/tag/03EY">7.1.2.1</a>, the morphism $e: K \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X,Y)$ exhibits $X$ as a power of $Y$ by $K$ in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ if and only if the morphism </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  e^{\operatorname{op}}: K^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X,Y)^{\operatorname{op}} \simeq \operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} }( Y, X ) \]
</div>
<p> exhibits $X$ as a copower of $Y$ by $K^{\operatorname{op}}$ in the opposite $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}}$. </p>
</article>
